# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the maintainer's Windows machine, so without this
# every checkout would produce CRLF files that the mixed-line-ending pre-commit
# hook rewrites back to LF on the next commit — a loop that fails the first
# commit attempt every time. Pinning eol=lf keeps the working tree identical on
# Windows, macOS and CI runners.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated. Collapsed by default in GitHub diffs so a 3,400-line lockfile does
# not bury the reviewable part of a pull request.
uv.lock linguist-generated=true
